", "target": ["t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "ISA.12.6.a010", "note": "As the rectum of the construct noun, the suffix is rendered of thee.", "source": ["WLC.ISA.12.6.010"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.12.6.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014", "t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "ISA.12.6.a011", "note": "The anarthrous substantival adjective takes the supplied the and generic One, but heads on Holy, which carries its lexeme.", "source": ["WLC.ISA.12.6.011"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.12.6.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017", "t018", "t019"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "ISA.12.6.a012", "note": "The construct relation belongs to the nomen rectum Israel.", "source": ["WLC.ISA.12.6.012"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.12.6.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020", "t021"], "target_head": "t021"}], "ref": "ISA.12.6", "review_notes": ["The source's feminine singular inhabitant corresponds to the briefing's Hebrew gloss inhabitress, while the ASV uses the unmarked English inhabitant."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
